<Base title="Community guidelines" description="How to take part in the IntoTheTwilightZone.com forums and fan contributions: be kind, stay on topic, mark spoilers, share only what you have the right to share.">
  <article class="legal">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/community/">Community</a> / Guidelines</p>
    <h1>Community guidelines</h1>
    <p class="lead">This is a place for fans of every age and every era of the Zone, from people who watched the first broadcasts to people who found it last week. Keep it a place they all want to come back to.</p>
    <h2>Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Be kind and assume good faith.</strong> Disagree about episodes as much as you like; don't make it personal.</li>
      <li><strong>Mark spoilers.</strong> Many episodes turn on their ending. Say "Spoiler:" and leave a blank line before revealing a twist, especially in topic titles, which should never give an ending away.</li>
      <li><strong>Back up facts.</strong> When you correct or add something, say where it comes from.</li>
      <li><strong>Post in the right forum</strong>, and search before starting a topic that may already exist. Record pages have a Discuss link that finds topics about them.</li>
      <li><strong>Credit others.</strong> Name the artist, writer or photographer whose work you're talking about.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Don't</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No harassment, hate or threats</strong>, including about people's race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability or age.</li>
      <li><strong>No sexual or graphic violent content.</strong> Discussing a story's themes is fine; posting explicit material is not.</li>
      <li><strong>No spam or advertising.</strong> The site is non-commercial: no selling, shop links, affiliate codes or self-promotion beyond sharing your own fan work.</li>
      <li><strong>No piracy.</strong> Don't upload or link to unauthorised copies of episodes, films, books, music or scripts.</li>
      <li><strong>No private information.</strong> Don't post anyone's address, phone number, email or other personal details, including your own.</li>
      <li><strong>No impersonation</strong> of cast, crew, their families, rights holders or the site's staff.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How moderation works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A new member's first two posts are checked by a moderator before they appear. After that, posts appear straight away.</li>
      <li>Every upload and suggestion is checked before it appears.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>Report</strong> on any post, topic, contribution or profile that breaks these guidelines. Reports are private.</li>
      <li>Moderators may hide posts, close or move topics, and suspend accounts. Repeated or serious problems mean a suspension.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
